From 54b21917213a9413ddfa93e98928a820cb81b457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:14:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/23] Foveation: medium_plus preset between medium and light,
 and a bench --fov flag

foveated_encoding_preset = medium_plus is centre 0.50x0.45 with edges 4x5:
2752x1216 encoded for 2160x2160 eyes, 17 percent more pixels than medium
(2560x1120); light is 3456x1536. It travels as FoveationPreset::Medium with
its own centre and edge parameters in the stream announce, so no protocol
change; CalculateFoveationLayout gains an explicit-parameters overload and
StreamingServer computes every layout through ConfiguredFoveationLayout.
Existing preset names and their layouts are unchanged; default stays off.

Measured on the M5 Pro low-latency encoder, scene pattern, 50 Mbps,
encoder_min_qp 12, sparse submits beside the live stream: callback p50
medium 10.1-10.2 ms, medium_plus 10.8-11.0, light 14.3-14.5. Sustained 90 Hz
bench runs share the media engine with the live stream and were 18 ms even
for medium, so whether medium_plus holds 90 Hz live is not yet measured.

